@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+{
+  "file": "prompts/greet.prompt",
+  "snippet": "Write a short, friendly, one-sentence welcome for the customer named {{custmerName}}.",
+  "cause": "The greet prompt template references the variable {{custmerName}} (misspelled), which is never supplied because the greet flow passes customerName, so the rendered prompt has no name and the model produces a generic welcome.",
+  "evidence": "src/flows.ts passes { customerName } to ai.prompt('greet'), and the prompt's input schema declares customerName, but prompts/greet.prompt line 7 uses {{custmerName}}; that placeholder renders empty, so the prompt reads 'named .' and the model has no name to address. The other customers get the same output because every call drops the name the same way. The fix changes the placeholder to {{customerName}}."
+}
